Verified triage and fixes (2026-10-16)
======================================

Fixed in this pass
------------------
- Waste pickup showed a Rate button for volunteer suggestions that have no
  WasteCollector record ID. Removed that non-working action for suggestions;
  saved WasteCollector records retain the working rating action.
- Existing collector reviews could be retrieved from the ratings endpoint but
  were not visible from the collector list. Added an expandable View reviews
  control for saved collectors, with loading, empty, retry, and error states.
  Review text is rendered as text content. Added responsive review-card styles
  and Bangla/English button labels.
- Added a Selenium check covering saved collector reviews, the absence of the
  volunteer Rate button, and mobile-width horizontal overflow.

Previously reported items checked
---------------------------------
- Second-hand goods interest: the detail-page button calls the existing
  interest endpoint, and the endpoint prevents duplicate/self interest. The
  backend test and existing browser interest/contact test passed. No further
  fix was needed.
- NID verification submission: the form calls the existing submit/status APIs.
  The existing ST 12 browser scenario passed (missing-file validation and
  pending status). No further fix was needed.
- Volunteer duplicate signup (S4-T12): the backend rejects duplicate signups
  with HTTP 400, covered by the Django volunteer test. The old Selenium case
  opens `/volunteer.html`; the current app route is `/volunteer-opportunities/`
  and its signup actions are rendered from the API. Treat the old browser case
  as a stale route assumption, not evidence to change the working signup API.
- Waste collector source: `/api/waste/collectors/available/` intentionally
  lists Volunteer-role users. `/api/waste/collectors/` lists community-shared
  collector records; the UI identifies their submitter as "Shared by". No evidence
  supports changing those role rules; this remains a product-rule question.

Remaining test discrepancy
--------------------------
- The live-server `test_collector_rating_and_report` exposed a real mismatch:
  it opens `/collector-details/?id=...` with a Volunteer User UUID, while the
  details page only used the WasteCollector-specific profile and rating APIs.
  The page now supports Volunteer profiles through the existing general user
  rating and report APIs. Phone and location are returned only when the
  volunteer enabled visibility. Saved WasteCollector records continue using
  the separate waste-rating API; their report form is hidden because that
  endpoint has no defined reported-user mapping. Django API regression tests
  cover volunteer profile access, privacy, and rejecting non-volunteer UUIDs.
- The targeted Selenium rerun could not start Chrome in this environment
  (`DevToolsActivePort file doesn't exist`; Selenium Manager cache access was
  denied), so browser confirmation of the repaired rating/report flow remains
  unverified here. The prior failure was a real app contract issue; this rerun
  failure is an environment issue.
- The full pytest run completed with 86 passed and one unrelated failure:
  goods listing image persistence raised `PermissionError` creating its
  temporary `goods_images` directory under the Windows temp root. The focused
  waste suite passed (12 tests), so this failure did not involve this change.

UI and goods interest fixes
---------------------------
- Verification approve/reject controls used the global full-width `.btn`
  rule inside a side-by-side action row, making labels overlap or buttons
  overflow. Scoped flex sizing, wrapping, and spacing now keep them usable.
- Admin volunteer filters now use a responsive grid. Volunteer opportunity,
  health question, and goods-list cards use wrapping action links and safe
  text wrapping at narrow widths.
- Goods detail now receives the authenticated user's existing interest state.
  After interest is recorded the action stays disabled and shows a translated
  “Interest sent” label after reload, while seller contact remains available
  through the existing privacy-gated detail response.
- Verification with Selenium is blocked in this Windows environment because
  Chrome crashes during startup (`DevToolsActivePort file doesn't exist`) and
  Selenium Manager cannot write its cache. Node.js is also unavailable, so
  JavaScript syntax checks could not be run here.
- The previous full Selenium run had 59 passed and 19 failed. Most failures
  came from `test_annotoma.py` and `test_mokarram.py`, which hard-code
  `127.0.0.1:8000`, depend on pre-seeded accounts/session state, or navigate
  legacy page URLs/selectors. These tests do not start the current Django live
  server. Do not treat their failures as confirmed current-app defects until
  run against the intended seeded server or migrated to live-server fixtures.
- Current stylesheet references inspected in frontend pages use the shared
  Django static `css/style.css` path. The existing farmer responsive browser
  case passed. A full visual review of every page at mobile and desktop sizes
  is still outstanding.
